  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Rain diminishes by this evening. \n\n-  A brief drying and warming trend is expected Wednesday and\n   Thursday. Fog or low clouds are possible each morning.\n\n-  Chance for frost in high valleys of southwest Montana.\n\n-  Unsettled with showers on Friday. Growing confidence for a wet\n   and cool system with high elevation snow developing by this\n   weekend, that may start as early as Friday.\n\nA drying trend comes into play late Tuesday into Wednesday.\nSeasonable temperatures in the mid 70s for many valley locations\nare anticipated. Chilly mornings and even some fog will feel very\nfall like to end the week.\n\nBeginning on Thursday, winds will increase from the west as zonal\n(westerly) flow develops ahead of the next approaching weather \nsystem. This could cause some increased chop on local lakes as \nwell as possibly enhancing fire weather concerns across far \nsouthwest Montana, which has largely been missed by the recent \nprecipitation event.\n\nA digging trough on Friday will bring showers to the region with\ncooler temperatures. This initial system may be a quick mover\nahead of the slower trough that is forecast to develop\nSaturday/Sunday which could bring more precipitation and high\nmountain snowfall. Highs during the weekend could range in the 50s\nand 60s. As the low pressure system approaches from the west,\nbreezy northeasterly winds could be possible on Saturday which\ncould be impactful to area lakes.",
